    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d226">

                <pb facs="0317" n="243" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg243"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/13332</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Special Representative</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">House</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-18T22:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 18, 1917, 10 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 11.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For the President:</p>
                <p>The following is short <hi rendition="#italic">résumé</hi> of the general
                    political conditions.</p>
                <p>Russia: Kerensky and other more
                    responsible officials urge Allies to make an offer of peace, basis no
                    annexations or indemnities. They believe Germany would not accept and this would
                    help to solidify Russia. They do not believe Germany would make separate peace
                    with Russia owing to danger of socialistic infection, but they believe Germany
                    will take Petrograd and near provinces in spring. They claim this would suit
                    German purposes better because demobilization of Russian Army would produce
                    anarchy and total loss stores of supplies. …</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edward House</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
